⏺ The design skill's guidance is loaded. Here's my design plan:

  - Subject: A rotating ellipse whose minor axis oscillates at exactly 5× the
    rotation frequency — an instrument/drafting subject. The 5:1 ratio is the
    page's identity and gets carried as content (live readouts, the formula, the
    trace).
  - Color: Cool technical palette, not the usual warm-cream default — blue-grey
    paper #F2F4F8, drafting blue accent #3157D5, amber trace #D97706 (light);
    matched dark set.
  - Type: Instrument Sans for UI text (an instrument face for an instrument
    page) + IBM Plex Mono for measured values and section labels — the
    engraved-panel vernacular of drafting instruments.
  - Layout: Canvas stage with three live readout chips (rotation, minor axis,
    5:1 ratio) beside a controls panel grouped into Axes / Motion / Display,
    formula in the footer.

